m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Serine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: The network converges on protected serine precursors rather than attempting to accumulate free serine immediately. Glycolaldehyde is the main soluble C2 hub and is accessed independently by surface formaldehyde dimerization or hydrothermal reduction of glyoxal; once trapped in cooler concentrating pools or mineral pores, it enters either Strecker chemistry to serine nitrile or a Bucherer-Bergs-type hydantoin manifold. Serine is then released by overall or stepwise hydrolysis. A lower-confidence but chemically motivated parallel branch first makes glycine nitrile from formaldehyde and then homologates it with formaldehyde to serine nitrile.\n\nMOLECULES (14 nodes):\n  - mol_001: CH2O (formaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_002: C2H2O2 (glyoxal) [starting]\n  - mol_003: H2 (hydrogen) [starting]\n  - mol_004: C2H4O2 (glycolaldehyde) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_005: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_006: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_007: H2O (water) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_008: C3H6N2O (serine nitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C3H8N2O2 (serinamide) [intermediate]\n  - mol_010: CO2 (carbon dioxide) [starting]\n  - mol_011: C4H6N2O3 (5-hydroxymethylhydantoin) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_012: C4H8N2O4 (N